    <DataNode elementId="AT2G13360-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G13360-MONOMER" type="Protein" groupRef="CPLX-2082">
      <Xref identifier="Q56YA5" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900.0" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">In Arabidopsis, the donor for aminotransfer can either be a serine or a glutamate |CITS: [11154287]|. Serine:glyoxylate aminotransferase encoded by AGT1 is a homodimer. The purified recombinant protein has the highest activity with the serine:glyoxylate transamination. It also catalyzed alanine:glyoxylate transamination and serine:pyruvate transamination with much lower specific activity.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G13360-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G13360.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Mint" value="Q56YA5" />
