      <Comment source="BioCyc">This reaction converts serine to glycine, and is also a major source of one-carbon units for the cell.</Comment>
      <Comment source="BioCyc">This reaction converts serine to glycine, and is also a major source of one-carbon addition for the cell. The enzyme is a pyridoxal-phosphate protein. It also catalyses the reaction of glycine with acetaldehyde to form L-threonine, and with 4-trimethylammoniobutanal to form 3-hydroxy-N6,N6,N6-trimethyl-L-lysine.</Comment>
